      "writtenOn": "2017-03-03T01:43:40Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Turns out ArrayList has a contains() method. Comparing to HashSet.contains()\u0027s O(1) performance, ArrayList.contains() is O(n). However, in our use case ArrayList does have an advantage over HashSet since WifiNative.RoamingConfig can take the ArrayList as is.\n\nFrom historical data, we know for majority of time this BSSID blacklist is empty and the performance of checking HashSet and ArrayList should be the same. I am leaning towards keeping it as an ArrayList and fixing WifiNetworkSelector to use contains() API instead of implementing our own.",
      "parentUuid": "aa3250df_01be19da",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 258,
        "startChar": 60,
        "endLine": 258,
        "endChar": 77
      },
      "revId": "af1ee09663c9a19ead56c08b84bfa9257cf80d40",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": false
    },
