      "writtenOn": "2017-03-03T05:53:26Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "something that might really help with separating the logic in this method is to make a private updateBlacklist method.  If that returns true, then you would write out the updated blacklist.  It could look something like:\n\npublic boolean trackBssid(...) {\n   boolean updated \u003d updateBlacklist(...);\n   if (updated \u0026\u0026 fwroam) {\n       write config\n    }\n \n    ....  do other one off stuff\n}\n\nThis would let you separate the logic of maintaining the blacklist from what happens when the blacklist is updated.",
      "range": {
